{%- comment -%}
  ow-brand-colors — the OWV2 named brand palette as CSS custom properties.

  Fixed brand accents that are NOT tied to a per-section merchant color
  setting (e.g. the Sunbrella savings badge, the Electric product-card
  border) belong here, referenced as var(--ow-<name>), so the hex lives in
  exactly one place instead of being re-typed in every section that needs
  it. A section's own color SETTINGS (background_color, text_color,
  card_background, ...) still take a literal hex "default" in their schema
  -- Shopify's color picker cannot default to a CSS variable -- but those
  defaults are chosen to match the tokens below, so a freshly added section
  instance starts on-palette.

  Rendered from layout/theme.liquid and layout/password.liquid, alongside
  ow-fonts. Unlike ow-fonts, there is no vendor token this overrides, so
  render order relative to css-variables does not matter.

  Names and hex confirmed so far: Electric, Sand, Sunbrella, Midnight.
  Wonderland / Salmon / Purple Haze / Solar Flare are pending confirmation
  of which hex maps to which name -- do not guess and add them here.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  :root {
    --ow-electric: #FF3F00;
    --ow-sand: #F7F5F1;
    --ow-sunbrella: #FBB925;
    --ow-midnight: #00180C;
  }
</style>
